<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>PEB Estimate Assistant</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="shell">

  <aside class="sidebar">
    <div class="brand">
      <div class="brand-mark">PEB</div>
      <div>
        <div class="brand-title">Estimate Assistant</div>
        <div class="brand-sub">offline / draft tool</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <nav class="side-nav">
      <button class="nav-item active" data-tab="estimate">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 4h16v16H4z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 13h8M8 17h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>New Estimate</span>
      </button>
      <button class="nav-item" data-tab="history">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M12 8v5l3 2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>Historical Projects</span>
        <span class="count-pill" id="histCount">0</span>
      </button>
      <button class="nav-item" data-tab="drawing">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 20h18M6 20V9l6-5 6 5v11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <span>Drawing Preview</span>
      </button>
      <button class="nav-item" data-tab="ai">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M12 2v4M12 18v4M2 12h4M18 12h4M5 5l3 3M16 16l3 3M19 5l-3 3M8 16l-3 3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>AI Assistant</span>
      </button>
      <button class="nav-item" data-tab="about">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M12 8h.01M11 12h1v5h1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>About &amp; Method</span>
      </button>
    </nav>

    <div class="sidebar-foot">
      <div class="db-status" id="dbStatus">Connecting to local database…</div>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <main class="content">

    <div class="banner">
      <strong>Preliminary estimate only — not for construction.</strong>
      Every output here is a draft for your engineer to review and approve. This tool does not
      perform wind/seismic analysis, member design, or connection design, and does not read DWG files.
    </div>

    <!-- ===================== TAB: ESTIMATE ===================== -->
    <section class="tab active" id="tab-estimate">

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Step 1 — Offline file parse (optional)</h2>
        <label>Upload a PIF / Estimate worksheet (.xlsx, .pdf, or .txt) — regex-based, fully offline</label>
        <input type="file" id="offlineFile" accept=".xlsx,.xls,.pdf,.txt,.csv">
        <div class="actions"><button class="btn secondary" onclick="parseOffline()">Scan file for fields</button></div>
        <div class="note" id="offlineStatus"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Step 2 — Building parameters</h2>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="field"><label>Project / building name</label><input type="text" id="name" value="New Project"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Frame type (e.g. CS, MS1)</label><input type="text" id="frame_type" value="CS"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Width, out-to-out (m)</label><input type="number" id="width" value="45.72" step="0.01"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Length (m)</label><input type="number" id="length" value="60" step="0.01"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Eave height (m)</label><input type="number" id="eave_height" value="9" step="0.01"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Number of bays</label><input type="number" id="bay_count" value="8" step="1" min="1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Roof slope, rise : run</label>
            <div class="row-inline"><input type="number" id="slope_rise" value="1.5" step="0.1"><span>:</span><input type="number" id="slope_run" value="10" step="0.1"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="field"><label>Wind speed (km/h, 3‑sec gust)</label><input type="number" id="wind_speed" value="130" step="1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Roof live load (kN/m²)</label><input type="number" id="live_load" value="0.57" step="0.01"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Collateral load (kN/m²)</label><input type="number" id="collateral" value="0.1" step="0.01"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Seismic zone</label><input type="text" id="seismic_zone" value="Zone 3"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Occupancy category</label>
            <select id="occupancy"><option>I</option><option selected>II</option><option>III</option><option>IV</option></select>
          </div>
          <div class="field"><label>Enclosure</label>
            <select id="enclosure"><option>Open</option><option>Partially Enclosed</option><option selected>Enclosed</option></select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Step 3 — Special items</h2>

        <div class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" id="has_mezz"><label for="has_mezz">Mezzanine / platform</label></div>
        <div class="subgrid" id="mezzGrid">
          <div class="field"><label>Mezzanine floor area (m²)</label><input type="number" id="mezz_area" value="0" step="1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Assumed rate (kg/m²)</label><input type="number" id="mezz_rate" value="45" step="1"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="check-row" style="margin-top:12px"><input type="checkbox" id="has_crane"><label for="has_crane">Crane system</label></div>
        <div class="subgrid" id="craneGrid">
          <div class="field"><label>Crane capacity (tons)</label><input type="number" id="crane_cap" value="0" step="0.5"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Runway length (m)</label><input type="number" id="crane_len" value="0" step="1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Assumed rate (kg per ton·m)</label><input type="number" id="crane_rate" value="3.5" step="0.1"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="check-row" style="margin-top:12px"><input type="checkbox" id="has_canopy"><label for="has_canopy">Canopy / roof extension</label></div>
        <div class="subgrid" id="canopyGrid">
          <div class="field"><label>Canopy area (m²)</label><input type="number" id="canopy_area" value="0" step="1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Assumed rate (kg/m²)</label><input type="number" id="canopy_rate" value="8" step="1"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Step 4 — Main-material breakdown assumption (%)</h2>
        <p class="note">Averaged from real Estimate Worksheets. Adjust if your jobs run differently — normalized to 100% automatically.</p>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="field"><label>Built-up frames (BU)</label><input type="number" id="pct_bu" value="38"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Deep sections / welded (DSW)</label><input type="number" id="pct_dsw" value="11"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Secondary members / bracing (SP)</label><input type="number" id="pct_sp" value="9"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Purlins &amp; girts (cold-formed)</label><input type="number" id="pct_cf" value="15"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Roof + wall sheeting</label><input type="number" id="pct_rs" value="14"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Accessories / bolts / trims</label><input type="number" id="pct_acc" value="13"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="flex-between">
          <h2 style="margin:0">Step 5 — Calculate</h2>
          <div class="actions">
            <button class="btn primary" onclick="runEstimate()">Calculate Estimate</button>
            <button class="btn secondary" id="csvBtn" style="display:none" onclick="downloadCSV()">Download CSV</button>
            <button class="btn secondary" id="saveHistBtn" style="display:none" onclick="saveCurrentAsHistory()">Save as historical record…</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="resultsBox"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== TAB: HISTORY ===================== -->
    <section class="tab" id="tab-history">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Historical projects (SQLite database)</h2>
        <p class="note">The estimator predicts kg/m² by comparing a new building against these records, weighted by
        similarity in width, eave height, wind speed, live load, and enclosure. Two example records come from your
        uploaded Estimate Worksheets. Add your own completed jobs' <em>actual</em> weights to improve accuracy — this
        is stored locally in <code>peb_estimator.db</code>, not sent anywhere.</p>
        <div id="historyTableWrap"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== TAB: DRAWING ===================== -->
    <section class="tab" id="tab-drawing">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Schematic anchor bolt plan (preview only)</h2>
        <p class="note">Uses Width / Length / Bay count from the New Estimate tab.</p>
        <div id="planSvgWrap"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Schematic cross section (preview only)</h2>
        <div id="sectionSvgWrap"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="actions"><button class="btn secondary" onclick="drawSchematics()">Refresh from current form</button></div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== TAB: AI ===================== -->
    <section class="tab" id="tab-ai">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>AI Assistant — draft parameters &amp; notes from any file</h2>
        <p class="note">Upload a PIF, PPD, or EST file (xlsx, pdf, image, or text). The AI drafts building parameters
        and a short engineering summary. Requires <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> in your local <code>.env</code> file —
        everything else in this app works without it. Output is always a <strong>DRAFT for your engineer to review</strong>.</p>

        <label>Upload PIF / PPD / EST file</label>
        <input type="file" id="aiFile" accept=".pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.xlsx,.xls,.txt,.csv">

        <label style="margin-top:10px">Notes for the AI (optional)</label>
        <input type="text" id="aiNote" placeholder="e.g. this is Bldg B02, mirror image of B01, add a 5T crane">

        <div class="actions"><button class="btn primary" onclick="sendToAI()">Analyze with AI (draft)</button></div>
        <div class="note" id="aiStatus"></div>
        <div id="aiOutput" style="margin-top:14px"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== TAB: ABOUT ===================== -->
    <section class="tab" id="tab-about">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>How this works</h2>
        <p><strong>1. Weight prediction.</strong> Inverse-distance-weighted nearest neighbours over your historical
        projects (width, eave height, wind speed, live load, enclosure) predict a kg/m² rate; multiplied by area for
        the base weight. With no history, a rule-of-thumb formula is used instead.</p>
        <p><strong>2. Special items.</strong> Mezzanine, crane and canopy weight are added using simple per-unit rates
        you can edit — not derived from load analysis.</p>
        <p><strong>3. Category split.</strong> Base weight is divided into Built-up / Deep-section / Secondary members
        / Purlins &amp; girts / Sheeting / Accessories using your percentages.</p>
        <p><strong>4. Drawing preview.</strong> A schematic anchor-bolt grid and cross-section from your basic
        dimensions, for visual sanity-checking only.</p>
        <h2>What this deliberately does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No wind/seismic load-combination analysis or joint reactions</li>
          <li>No member sizing, deflection checks, or connection design</li>
          <li>No DWG parsing</li>
          <li>No generation of certified/stamped drawings</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Everything here is meant to speed up early budgeting before your engineering team runs the real structural
        design in your normal software, and before a licensed engineer reviews and approves it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</div>

<script src="/static/js/drawing.js"></script>
<script src="/static/js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
